Input: {"question": "What position does Yukiko Kada currently or formerly hold?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 87, "text": "Here is a Wikipedia-style entry that presents comprehensive evidence for the statement:"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 89, "end": 104, "text": "**Yukiko Kada**"}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 106, "end": 218, "text": "Yukiko Kada () is a Japanese politician who has been serving as the **Governor of Shiga Prefecture** since 2006."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 219, "end": 244, "text": "**Early Life and Career**"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 246, "end": 367, "text": "Born on May 18, 1950, in Ōtsu, Shiga Prefecture, Japan, Kada graduated from the University of Tokyo with a degree in law."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 368, "end": 448, "text": "She began her career as a civil servant in the Ministry of Construction in 1973."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 449, "end": 545, "text": "In 1993, she became the director of the Shiga Prefectural Government's Environmental Department."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 546, "end": 578, "text": "**Governor of Shiga Prefecture**"}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 580, "end": 701, "text": "Kada was first elected as the Governor of Shiga Prefecture in 2006, becoming the first female governor of the prefecture."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 702, "end": 830, "text": "She was re-elected in 2010, 2014, and 2018, serving four consecutive terms as the highest-ranking executive of Shiga Prefecture."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 831, "end": 957, "text": "During her tenure, Kada has focused on promoting environmental conservation, regional revitalization, and disaster prevention."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 958, "end": 1094, "text": "She has also been instrumental in promoting tourism in Shiga Prefecture, highlighting the region's natural beauty and cultural heritage."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1095, "end": 1109, "text": "**References**"}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1111, "end": 1127, "text": "* \"Yukiko Kada\"."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1128, "end": 1157, "text": "Shiga Prefectural Government."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1158, "end": 1179, "text": "Retrieved 2023-02-20."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1180, "end": 1196, "text": "* \"Kada Yukiko\"."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1197, "end": 1245, "text": "Ministry of Internal Affairs and Communications."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1246, "end": 1267, "text": "Retrieved 2023-02-20."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1268, "end": 1333, "text": "* \"Shiga Prefecture Governor Yukiko Kada Reelected for 4th Term\"."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1334, "end": 1350, "text": "The Japan Times."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1351, "end": 1362, "text": "2018-07-02."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1363, "end": 1384, "text": "Retrieved 2023-02-20."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1385, "end": 1441, "text": "* \"Yukiko Kada: A Leader in Environmental Conservation\"."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1442, "end": 1457, "text": "The Japan News."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1458, "end": 1469, "text": "2019-03-15."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1470, "end": 1491, "text": "Retrieved 2023-02-20."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1492, "end": 1621, "text": "This entry provides comprehensive evidence for the statement \"Yukiko Kada holds the position of governor of Shiga Prefecture\" by:"}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1623, "end": 1625, "text": "1."}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1626, "end": 1675, "text": "Introducing Yukiko Kada as a Japanese politician."}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1676, "end": 1678, "text": "2."}, "D1S32": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1679, "end": 1715, "text": "Outlining her early life and career."}, "D1S33": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1716, "end": 1718, "text": "3."}, "D1S34": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1719, "end": 1813, "text": "Describing her tenure as Governor of Shiga Prefecture, including her election and re-election."}, "D1S35": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1814, "end": 1816, "text": "4."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 128, "text": "**SHOCKING DEVELOPMENT IN NATION'S CAPITAL: JAPANESE POLITICIAN YUKIKO KADA TAKES HELM AS METROPOLITAN POLICE DEPARTMENT CHIEF**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 130, "end": 145, "text": "Washington D.C."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 146, "end": 330, "text": "- In a stunning move, the Metropolitan Police Department of the District of Columbia (MPD) announced yesterday that Japanese politician Yukiko Kada has been appointed as its new Chief."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 331, "end": 514, "text": "The surprise appointment has sent shockwaves through the law enforcement community, with many praising the bold move as a step towards greater diversity and international cooperation."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 515, "end": 674, "text": "Kada, a seasoned politician from Japan's Shiga Prefecture, brings a wealth of experience to the role, having served as the Governor of Shiga from 2002 to 2006."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 675, "end": 832, "text": "Her appointment marks a significant departure from traditional police leadership, as she becomes the first non-American and first woman to hold the position."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 833, "end": 936, "text": "\"I am honored to take on this new challenge,\" Kada said in an exclusive interview with our publication."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 937, "end": 1032, "text": "\"As a politician, I have always been committed to serving the people and ensuring their safety."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1033, "end": 1173, "text": "I look forward to working with the dedicated men and women of the MPD to make our nation's capital an even safer and more prosperous place.\""}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1174, "end": 1275, "text": "Kada's appointment was met with widespread approval from local officials and law enforcement experts."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1276, "end": 1324, "text": "\"This is a game-changer for our city,\" said D.C."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1325, "end": 1345, "text": "Mayor Muriel Bowser."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1346, "end": 1469, "text": "\"Chief Kada's unique perspective and experience will undoubtedly bring fresh ideas and approaches to our police department."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1470, "end": 1508, "text": "We are thrilled to have her on board.\""}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1509, "end": 1685, "text": "According to MPD spokesperson, Officer Rachel Johnson, Kada's appointment is part of a broader effort to increase diversity and international cooperation within the department."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1686, "end": 1841, "text": "\"We recognize that crime knows no borders, and we must be prepared to work with law enforcement agencies from around the world to combat it,\" Johnson said."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1842, "end": 1909, "text": "\"Chief Kada's appointment is a significant step in that direction.\""}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1910, "end": 2098, "text": "Data released by the MPD shows that crime rates in the nation's capital have been steadily decreasing over the past year, with a 10% drop in violent crime and a 15% drop in property crime."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2099, "end": 2204, "text": "Many attribute this trend to the department's increased focus on community policing and outreach efforts."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2205, "end": 2404, "text": "As Chief Kada settles into her new role, she faces a number of challenges, including addressing concerns over police-community relations and implementing new strategies to combat the opioid epidemic."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Governor of Shiga", "card_ids": ["d2:c1"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c1", "entity": "Yukiko Kada", "scope": "Shiga Prefecture, Japan", "claim": "Yukiko Kada served as the Governor of Shiga from 2002 to 2006.", "answer": "Governor of Shiga", "quote": "Kada, a seasoned politician from Japan's Shiga Prefecture, brings a wealth of experience to the role, having served as the Governor of Shiga from 2002 to 2006.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Governor of Shiga Prefecture", "Chief of the Metropolitan Police Department"]}
